---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArticleSchema from "../../components/ArticleSchema.astro";
import FaqSection from "../../components/FaqSection.astro";
import { site, description } from "../../content";
const path = "/guides/deliverability";
const title = "Diagnose Shopify email delivery before changing tools";
const desc = "Use authentication, recipient history and mailbox-level evidence to locate failures.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does switching platforms guarantee inbox placement?",
    "answer": "No. Authentication, audience history, content, recipient response and sending behavior remain relevant across migrations."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is a footer unsubscribe link enough?",
    "answer": "It serves a different interface from header-based one-click unsubscribe. Check the current mailbox rules that apply to your sending scope and test both paths."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a seed message prove deliverability?",
    "answer": "It can expose configuration or rendering issues, but it cannot prove placement across all customer accounts."
  },
  {
    "question": "How quickly should volume increase?",
    "answer": "Use the observed baseline, provider guidance and diagnostic capacity. This guide does not prescribe a universal volume or timetable."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/guides">← All operator guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Diagnose Shopify email delivery before changing tools</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Use authentication, recipient history and mailbox-level evidence to locate failures.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Draw the sender map</h2><p>List every system sending campaigns, cart reminders, account notices, review requests and shipping updates. For each, record visible From domain, return-path domain, DKIM signing domain, IP arrangement, suppression owner and accountable operator. Distinguish accepted delivery from inbox placement: a receiving server accepting a message does not prove that a person saw it. A platform migration alone does not repair recipient expectations or reputation.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Verify the applicable mailbox rules</h2><p>Google distinguishes requirements for all senders from additional requirements for bulk senders to personal Gmail accounts. Its guidance recommends SPF, DKIM and DMARC, and requires one-click unsubscribe for applicable bulk marketing/subscribed messages. Yahoo also specifies bulk-sender authentication and one-click unsubscribe controls. Read each current policy for scope and implementation details rather than treating a footer link as a header-level unsubscribe mechanism. Authentication is necessary operational work, not an inbox guarantee.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Inspect the message that actually arrived</h2><p>In controlled seed accounts, inspect full headers for authentication results and domain alignment. Compare them with DNS and the actual sender configuration; a green dashboard for a different subdomain is insufficient. Test the body unsubscribe link and mailbox one-click mechanism independently. Save the message ID, sender configuration version and resulting suppression state. Review reply routing and rejection logs as well. Seed checks reveal configuration failures; they do not measure placement for the whole customer base.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Separate technical rejection from audience rejection</h2><p>Group SMTP failures by enhanced status code and recipient domain. A persistent authentication failure needs configuration repair; temporary deferrals need provider-specific diagnosis and retry review. High complaints after a new signup source call for a capture/content investigation. Do not repeatedly resend to hard-bouncing or opted-out addresses. Inspect whether signup incentives, old imports or duplicate identities caused recipients to receive unexpected messages.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Use Shopify events to reduce irrelevant sends</h2><p>Test a purchase arriving after cart enrollment but before dispatch, a refunded order, cancelled subscription and an unavailable variant. Recheck current eligibility and product links at send time where the integration supports it. Maintain separate message ownership for genuine service notices and promotions. Yahoo recommends separating bulk marketing infrastructure from transactional/user mail; review the actual domains and IPs with the sending operator rather than assuming a label in an editor creates that separation.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Proposed controlled rollout</h2><p>Begin with a clearly eligible audience with recent, relevant activity, after configuration and suppression checks pass. Choose initial volume and increases from the store baseline, provider constraints and diagnostic capacity; no universal daily doubling schedule is prescribed. Log delivered, deferred, rejected, complaint and unsubscribe signals by mailbox domain and capture source. Pause expansion when unexplained deterioration appears. This is a proposed procedure, not an executed warmup or a claim that a fixed pilot duration proves safety.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Keep a decision log, not just a blended rate</h2><p>Record the denominator for every rate and which recipients the provider can observe. Compare like-for-like flows and time windows; a changing recipient mix can move a blended rate without any configuration change. Use clicks, orders, refunds and support reports alongside delivery diagnostics. A high open rate does not establish inbox placement or consent. For commercial impact, a properly designed no-send control can help distinguish attributed orders from incremental ones.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Choose the control surface</h2><p>A campaign-led store should demonstrate audience exclusions and unsubscribe behavior. A lifecycle-heavy store should demonstrate event freshness, purchase exits and cross-channel coordination. A developer-owned sender needs bounce callbacks, retry handling and operational escalation. A capture specialist must hand permission and source history to the primary sender. Evaluate Sequenzy or another candidate against the same recorded cases; no vendor ranking or current feature promise is made here.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Incident response and release evidence</h2><p>Pause the affected promotional source while preserving necessary service ownership. Save message IDs, provider responses, recent configuration changes and capture cohorts before changing multiple variables. Fix the diagnosed cause, rerun controlled checks and release a contained audience with an owner monitoring it. Avoid moving the whole file to another domain to evade a reputation problem. Document remaining uncertainty and rollback conditions before wider sending.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Primary references and related decisions</h2><p>Primary guidance checked 24 November 2026; scope is limited to the points attributed above. Store configuration and jurisdiction-specific review remain necessary.</p><ul><li><a class="link" href="https://support.google.com/mail/answer/81126">Google sender guidelines</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://senders.yahooinc.com/best-practices/">Yahoo sender best practices</a></li></ul><p><a class="link" href="/guides/consent-compliance">Consent compliance</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/discount-discipline">Discount discipline</a> · <a class="link" href="/guides/flow-collision-prevention">Flow collision prevention</a></p></div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
